<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  PLAYER overflow menu. Two rows as of G3.

  Source: canonical `Menu / Плеер` 2444:18763 (206x264, r20, `menuSurface` on a
  1px `menuOutline`), widened to 260 by the frozen proposal
  `sleep-timer-menu-active` 2517:2093 whose note is explicit - "The canonical menu
  is 206 wide, which cannot hold a label plus a trailing value. Widened to 260.
  This is the only change proposed to the existing menu."

  ## Two rows of the frozen four

  The frozen menu has four, in this order: Найти трек, **Таймер сна**, **Сообщить
  о проблеме**, История эфира. The two in bold exist and are drawn; the other two
  do not exist and are absent rather than inert.

  That rule is not new here. An inert row is tolerable when it names a feature the
  app genuinely has and cannot reach yet - `Row / Аватар` on
  profile-authenticated - and is not tolerable when it names a feature with no
  implementation behind it at all, because it is then a dead control asserting
  that something exists. `SleepTimerSurfacesTest` has held it since G2 and still
  does; only the membership of its two lists moved.

  The two shipping rows keep their frozen **relative order**. Nothing is promoted
  to close the gap left by Найти трек: the menu is the frozen menu with two rows
  missing, not a new two-row menu.

  ## Geometry, and the debt G2 recorded being paid

  All of it from screens-3.6.6/spec/primitives.mjs:184, the frozen menu primitive
  both menus are authored on:

      menu            260 wide, r20, 10 top pad, 50 bottom pad
      row             238x48 at x=11, pitch 52
      icon slot       48 at x=12 in the row, 24 glyph centred in it
      label           x=70, 15/22 Medium
      trailing        x=160, w=70, 14/20 on `primary`

  G2 shipped **10 / 10** rather than the frozen 10 / 50, by owner decision and for
  exactly as long as the menu carried one row: under a single 48dp line the 50 is
  40dp of unexplained space. It recorded that as temporary in three places and
  named the condition for repaying it - docs/SLEEP-TIMER-3.6.6.md §1, verbatim:
  "**Restoring `player_overflow_menu_pad_bottom` to 50dp is part of shipping the
  next Player action.**"

  G3 is that action, so the padding is the frozen 50 again and the menu is
  10 + 2x52 + 46 = **160** tall - which is exactly the frozen two-row
  `Menu / Коллекция` at 260x160. `SleepTimerSurfacesTest` measured the temporary
  68 and now measures the 160; that is how the debt was kept from being forgotten
  quietly, and it worked.

  ## The whole menu is absent in a build with no report endpoint

  Not this row alone - see PlayerOverflowMenu. A build without `report.properties`
  draws the one-row menu G2 shipped, and there the 10 / 10 padding is applied
  again, because it is again the right geometry for the surface being drawn.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/player_overflow_root"
    android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_menu_width"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:background="@drawable/bg_player_overflow_menu"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:paddingTop="@dimen/player_overflow_menu_pad_top"
    android:paddingBottom="@dimen/player_overflow_menu_pad_bottom">

    <!-- `Menu row / Таймер сна`, the second row of the frozen four and the only
         one whose feature exists. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/player_overflow_sleep_timer"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_row_height"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
        android:clickable="true"
        android:focusable="true"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_slot_inset"
        android:paddingEnd="0dp">

        <ImageView
            android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_slot"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_slot"
            android:contentDescription="@null"
            android:scaleType="center"
            android:src="@drawable/ic_sleep_timer_clock" />

        <!--
          Label at x=70 in a row whose content starts at 12: the 48 slot ends at
          60, so the frozen gap is 10. Width is what is left after the trailing
          value's 70 - the frozen `w - 22 - 70 - 70` = 98 on a 260 menu - and the
          value is GONE rather than INVISIBLE when the timer is off, so the label
          takes the full 160 the frozen no-trailing rows have.
        -->
        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/player_overflow_sleep_timer_label"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/player_overflow_gap"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:text="@string/sleep_timer_title"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Medium.15_22"
            android:textColor="@color/text_primary" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/player_overflow_sleep_timer_trailing"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_trailing_width"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Regular.14_20"
            android:textColor="@color/primary"
            android:visibility="gone"
            tools:text="24 мин"
            tools:visibility="visible" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!--
      `Menu row / Сообщить о проблеме` 2517:2104, the third of the frozen four and
      the second whose feature exists (G3).

      52 pitch, so the 4dp gap sits between the two 48dp rows and neither of them
      carries a margin of its own. The glyph is `Icon / alert` in the menu's
      `textSecondary` rather than in `error`: it names an action, it is not a
      warning about one.

      No trailing value. Only Таймер сна has one in the frozen menu, and only when
      a timer is armed.
    -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/player_overflow_report_problem"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_row_height"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/player_overflow_row_gap"
        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
        android:clickable="true"
        android:focusable="true"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_slot_inset"
        android:paddingEnd="0dp">

        <ImageView
            android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_slot"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_slot"
            android:contentDescription="@null"
            android:scaleType="center"
            android:src="@drawable/ic_player_overflow_alert" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/player_overflow_report_problem_label"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/player_overflow_gap"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:text="@string/report_title"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Medium.15_22"
            android:textColor="@color/text_primary" />
    </LinearLayout>
</LinearLayout>
